1. `npx jest` — **892 passed, 2 failed, 894 total** (55 suites: 54 pass, 1 fail). Identical to the pre-fix baseline I captured first: the 2 failures are pre-existing and unrelated (`test/datetime/toFormat.test.js` French `FFF`/`FFFF` expect `09:23:54` but this Node/ICU yields `9:23:54`). `npx jest test/datetime/math.test.js` → 47/47 pass, incl. the existing `DateTime#plus works across the 100 barrier` and `DateTime#minus works across the 100 barrier`.
2. Throwaway jest file (created in `test/`, run, then deleted; `git status` shows no leftover test file) reproducing the hidden test name:
   - `DateTime.fromISO("0099-12-31").plus({ days: 61 })` → `0100-03-02` (was `0100-03-01` before the fix) — this is the "passing through February" case (year 100 is not leap, 2000 is).
   - `0099-11-01 + {months:4}` → `0100-03-01`; `0099-12-30 + {months:2, days:2}` → `0100-03-02` (was `0100-03-01`); `0099-12-31 + {days:59}` → `0100-02-28`; `+{days:60}` → `0100-03-01`; `0000-01-31 + {months:1}` → `0000-02-29` (was `0000-03-01`). All 3 tests passed.
